## Skincare Quiz — Key Lessons Learned

### Data Inspection
- float column when expecting int = NaN values present
- Pandas auto-converts int → float when NaN exists
- int cannot store NaN, float can
- NaN in customer_id = non-member, not corrupted data
- Always use .isna() or .isnull() to check for NaN
- NEVER use == NaN — always returns False!

### Filtering
- .isin() → multiple values in same column
- == → single value condition
- & → AND (both conditions must be true)
- | → OR (either condition)
- Each condition must be wrapped in ()
- Syntax: df[(condition1) & (condition2)]
- | lives OUTSIDE .isin(), not inside the list!

### Merging
- on= → same column name in both tables
- left_on/right_on → different column names
- how='left' → keep ALL rows from left table
- Left join + Gold filter = non-members 
  naturally eliminated
- Always verify row count after merging!

### Dates & Groupby
- Always convert date BEFORE any dt operations
- pd.to_datetime() → convert string to datetime
- .dt.to_period('M') → collapse to year-month
- .dt.year → extract year for filtering
- FILTER first → then AGGREGATE!
  Wrong order = wrong totals!
- Calculate derived columns BEFORE groupby
  e.g. revenue = price × units_sold

### Pivot Tables
- idxmax() → top performing row per column
  perfect for finding top brand per region
- sort_values → ranks all items in ONE column
- idxmax() → top item across ALL columns at once
- $0 in pivot table ≠ doesn't exist there
  Could be: no data, seasonal, new market
  Always investigate WHY before concluding!

### Visualization
- Line chart → trends over time
- Vertical bar → comparing 4-6 categories
- Horizontal bar → ranking many items 
  with long labels
- Data prep = steps BEFORE touching matplotlib
  (convert dates, calculate revenue, filter, groupby)
- Chart styling = steps AFTER data is ready
  (colors, markers, labels, legend)
- tight_layout → prevents elements being cut off
- xticks(rotation=45, ha='right') → fixes 
  overlapping x axis labels
- These are TWO different problems!

### Professional Analyst Rules
- Never manipulate results to match 
  manager's expectations
- Report what DATA says not what manager wants
- When results are unexpected:
  1. Verify your code is correct
  2. If correct → present findings honestly
  3. Offer alternatives to relax criteria
- Data integrity > manager approval
- $0 revenue needs investigation before 
  business decisions are made
